 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Instead of changing Vika's car tires after work, Max goes out for celebratory drinks with Denis and Kostya, then tiptoes home late at night with a flimsy excuse.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Пацаны, сегодня вечером отдыхаем!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Нагиев взял меня музыкантом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Поздравляю тебя, это отлично!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Только сидим недолго сегодня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Здравствуй, любимая моя жена.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты вообще на часы смотрел?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "А у меня же нет часов.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Викуля, ну прости меня, пожалуйста.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ладно, тихо заходи в дом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты колёса на машине поменял?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Нет, я их завтра поменяю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Там сегодня была огромная очередь.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's walk through the celebration and Max's late-night return home.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Пацаны, сегодня вечером отдыхаем!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Guys, tonight we are celebrating!' In casual speech among young men, 'patsany' means 'guys' or 'lads'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Нагиев взял меня музыкантом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Nagiyev hired me as a musician.' Here Max anchors the thought on 'took' and finishes on 'musician', keeping the spoken rhythm brisk and natural.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Поздравляю тебя, это отлично!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Congratulations, that is great!' Russian says 'I congratulate you' in the first-person singular where English uses the plural noun.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Только сидим недолго сегодня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Only we are not staying out long today.' Married men Kostya and Max both promise to head home early — and fail.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Здравствуй, любимая моя жена.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Hello, my beloved wife.' Stumbling home late, Max uses an overly sweet greeting.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты вообще на часы смотрел?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did you even look at the clock?' In Russian, a clock or watch is always a plural noun ('chasy').",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "А у меня же нет часов.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I do not even have a watch.' Russians say 'by me' or 'with us' where English says 'I have' or 'we have', without needing a separate word for 'have'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Викуля, ну прости меня, пожалуйста.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Vikulya, forgive me, please.' Max uses an affectionate diminutive of Vika's name to soften her anger.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ладно, тихо заходи в дом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Fine, come inside quietly.' Vika lets him in before asking the decisive question.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты колёса на машине поменял?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did you change the wheels on the car?' The neuter plural 'wheels' has the stress on the second syllable in the plural.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Нет, я их завтра поменяю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, I will change them tomorrow.' Caught unprepared, Max immediately pushes the task to 'tomorrow'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Там сегодня была огромная очередь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'There was a huge line there today.' Every Russian driver's classic excuse in autumn is the long queue at the tire shop. Now listen to the whole scene again at natural speed.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
